# Mosquitto ACL template — SHM platform
#
# The live `mosquitto/acl` and `mosquitto/passwd` files are NOT tracked in git:
# `passwd` stores hashed broker credentials, and both are owned by the broker
# uid (1883), which also makes `mosquitto/` unwritable by the developer account.
#
# To apply this template:
#   sudo cp docs/mosquitto-acl.example mosquitto/acl
#   sudo chown 1883:1883 mosquitto/acl && sudo chmod 640 mosquitto/acl
#
# To create or update a broker account:
#   docker run --rm -v "$PWD/mosquitto:/mosquitto/config" eclipse-mosquitto:2.0 \
#     mosquitto_passwd -b /mosquitto/config/passwd <user> <password>
#
# Principle (§10): topic names are a routing convention, never an authorization
# mechanism. The broker ACL is defence in depth; the backend remains the
# authoritative check on device identity and tenant ownership.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Backend ingest consumer — subscribes to device telemetry, republishes feeds.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
user shm-backend
topic read shm/ingest/#
topic write shm/feed/#

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Field gateways (Raspberry Pi / Node simulator) — publish telemetry only.
# Per-gateway credentials are issued at provisioning time; this entry is the
# shared development account only and must not be used in production.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
user shm-gateway
topic write shm/ingest/#

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE — a browser-facing account (`shm-web`) is deliberately absent.
#
# Browsers must NOT connect to this broker. A browser-held credential is
# readable in page source, and a `shm/feed/#` subscription spans every tenant,
# which defeats tenant isolation (audit finding SEC-1). Live data reaches the
# UI through an authenticated, tenant-filtered SSE stream served by the API
# (target architecture §13.3, delivered in slice 5).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
